\begin{slide}
UD Factorization
\begin{itemize}
  \item Based on Cholesky Decomposition
  \item Unit Triangular Matrices: $U$ has 1's on the diagonal and all 0's below the diagonal.  E.g.,
\[
U=\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 5 & 7 \\
0 & 1 & 3\\
0 & 0 & 1
\end{bmatrix}
\]
\end{itemize} 
\end{slide}

\begin{slide}
UD Factorization
\begin{itemize}
  \item Factor $HPH\trans + R$ as $UDU\trans$, where $U$ is unit upper triangular and $D$ is diagonal.
  \item This then allows us to "invert" $HPH\trans + R$ by solving the equation unit upper triangular equation $UDU\trans X=H$ for the matrix $X$, which will yield $X=\left[HPH\trans + R\right]^{-1}H$
  \item This last expression is used on the covariance update equation in $KH$
\end{itemize} 
\end{slide}
